  "description": "#6978 — redo of an undo whose `delete_block` found its block already deleted. Undoing O1 (the create) by ref after O2 deleted the block appends a reverse `delete_block` whose cascade tombstones nothing: its `Active` walk finds no live row, so the block keeps O2's `deleted_at`. The redo reverses that undo row into `RestoreBlock { deleted_at_ref: <the undo row's created_at> }`, which matches no row, so the block STAYS deleted. The mock restored it, reading the cohort off the block's own `deleted_at` rather than off the op that is reversed.",
